# Security Policy — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

## Reporting a vulnerability

**Email:** security@{{PROD_DOMAIN}}

**GPG encryption (recommended for sensitive reports):**
Key fingerprint: `{{GPG_FINGERPRINT}}`
Public key: https://keys.openpgp.org/search?q=security@{{PROD_DOMAIN}}

**What to include:**
- Description of the vulnerability
- Steps to reproduce (PoC if possible)
- Affected component (app / db / proxy / backup / ci-cd)
- CVSS score estimate if known
- Your contact for follow-up

**What NOT to include:** production data, real user PII — use synthetic data in PoC.

---

## Disclosure timeline

| CVSS Score | Severity | Fix deadline | Public disclosure |
|---|---|---|---|
| 9.0 – 10.0 | Critical | 7 days | After fix deployed |
| 7.0 – 8.9 | High | 30 days | After fix deployed |
| 4.0 – 6.9 | Medium | 90 days | Standard |
| 0.1 – 3.9 | Low | Next release | Standard |

**Standard disclosure:** 90-day coordinated disclosure (Google Project Zero model).
If patch not available within deadline, we will disclose with available mitigations.

**Response SLA:** Acknowledgement within 48h of report.

